  "readOnlyHint": true,
  "title": "Get Pick of the Day"
 },
 "description": "Get today's published Pick of the Day: the sports markets where graded (S/A/B) sharp money is positioned, frozen at publish time. Pro opens the explicitly designated free selection plus the first four non-free selections in publication order; Max opens every available daily selection, up to twenty. Read entitled `picks` in `publication_order` order; use stable decimal-string `pick_id` for identity, not deprecated `pick_rank`. `is_free_selection` designates account access and `supersedes_pick_id` records replacement lineage. `locked_picks` lists extra unresolved ranks with only pick_rank and required_tier=max; no game, participants, league, time, links, market identifiers or backed facts are exposed. Each pick carries the matchup, the backed side (pick_outcome_label), the frozen pre-game price and the return on the flat $1,000 stake (`stake_usd`, `return_usd`; `return_per_100` keeps the literal $100 basis), the sharp-money holders on that side, the top grade, CLV capture status, and the thesis. `scheduled_picks` contains only entitled selected-but-unreleased slots and preserves required release_at; unauthorized future ranks join the identity-free locked_picks descriptors instead. No market identity is revealed before publication.\n\nBefore any pick is released the tool returns an error carrying reason pick_not_released and a retry_at instant: schedule the next read from retry_at (or the earliest scheduled_picks.release_at) instead of polling. A current-day pick whose holder proof is not readable yet is listed in `proof_pending_picks` (pick_rank, release_at, kickoff, retry_at) while `picks` carries the proof-readable picks; the tool returns read_model_warming only when no entitled published pick has readable proof. If only Max-locked ranks have published, a successful state=none response carries picks=[], pick_count=0, locked_picks, and an upgrade action. This is not a proof-warming state.\n\nArgs: none\n\nReturns: The published pick set for the current product day (America/New_York), or a pick_not_released error with retry_at.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {},
  "type": "object"
 },
